{"title":"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Cheese)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Cheese)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy_🔥🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product of all positive real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> satisfying the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/665e0374832779ed4ff9a3c24964286cf1c93313.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt[20]{x^{\\log_{2026} x}} = 26x\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> is an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Find the number of positive integer divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Raising both sides to the power of 20, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1841669925d931ed36a1c043f1b61a744c93b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{\\log_{2026}x} = (26x)^{20}\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" /> Taking log base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> of both sides, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/6/686d746296658c7643b79419ff50d992cfe6184f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{2026}x = 20 \\log_{x}26+20\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"17\" /> Rewrite in log base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c294ca4a42b0c1dfc668867a8147cd5c83701c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\ln x}{\\ln 2026} = \\dfrac{20 \\ln 26}{\\ln x} + 20\\]\" width=\"182\" height=\"37\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/e/41e1b2946173db1032ec480af09b93bbfa309a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\ln x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />. Substituting and multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/6199acf9d25806d0a4beaf001cd36abd79fcc44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\cdot \\ln 2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faaddf5856de18b7f47efab600909bfddad1401c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2 = 20 \\ln 26 \\ln 2026 + 20 \\ln 2026 \\cdot y\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"19\" /> This becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c07c461d0b97b92c515f0ea657ce492d3272ae24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2 - 20  \\ln 2026 \\cdot y - 20 \\ln 26 \\ln 2026 = 0\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"19\" /> Note that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />. We wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95bb6ff2039fc800b127042c6cd00fde71ecb09a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\cdot x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/5/e55be27f46822be5e9d4e26ac54251181152206b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{y_1 + y_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" />. By Vieta's, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b6ac6637cb78d4ea1f8337e848da364c22612b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y_1 + y_2 = 20 \\ln 2026\\]\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d2189ba35f2514bfe4ccb91443a4d3ed407d7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[e^{y_1 + y_2} = e^{20 \\ln 2026} = (e^{\\ln 2026})^{20} = 2026^{20} = 1013^{20} \\cdot 2^{20}\\]\" width=\"420\" height=\"20\" /> Then our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e65e5c00c6fcf32ef8c28630496589a895b56fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[21 \\cdot 21 = \\boxed{441} \\text{. } \\square\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"23\" />\n~BrocSoc\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Raising both sides to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/540c019ed0681747f84912ae6556658a2ee2a023.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> power:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0af596fdbc97fa77d3ac37b719f8d0317eb3b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{\\log_{2026} x}=26^{20}x^{20}\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"15\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1afb83921dbb401f9668f82c2a79837e80563e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2026^u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"14\" />. Now the equation becomes:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57d3445466442ae573b895e5bce2c233ff8d815.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2026^{u^2}=26^{20}2026^{20u}\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a89bf4bf5076150e904066b7d461f7aaf0dba86b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2026^{u^2-20u}=26^{20}\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />\nThe sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad99798ec4c38e165cf517cb9e02b1c9e824103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, therefore the product of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bbb3c4fbe4d662a50ef1f233bb0add32e263c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{20}=2^{20}\\cdot 1013^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"163\" height=\"17\" /> which has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d047ac3f1a0209f038b426e9a35332985339eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{441}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> factors. \n</p><p>~ <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Zhenghua\" title=\"User:Zhenghua\">zhenghua</a>\n</p><p>Another version of solution 2 (more in depth) is found in solution 5.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Cheese.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Cheese)\">Solution 3 (Cheese)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Cheese)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Just guess <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73df736c4b5a91adb6986579917f0a43931aa466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c5c4ef7ac854af9d74a8f9a3600296888b0b253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" />.\nEach of these have  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/1/101d7a2f74b5f3698f473a1152a0df8cdc5f9e46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 * 21 = \\boxed{441}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"118\" height=\"25\" /> factors.\n</p><p>~Aarav22 (I did not make AIME)\n</p><p>Note to author: it is not intuitively clear why one should guess these numbers, please provide more rationale\n</p><p>Note to note: there are actually not even that many to try. If we only use the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/262b5b6ed9571aa4b1d7cccbba6b580537f09e16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20,26, 2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />, and raise one to the power of another, we see that anything raised to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e513adf78ee28ac3403e90a42259bc55f59e2d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> will have way too many factors for the AIME answer extraction, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38a865f11c369c35ddb779d9c2b8c2ee7a3f55b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20^{26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"17\" /> also has too many factors for the answer extraction. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57e519f3722c6b4977e78866c9acd6c17db42287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{26}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, as it turns out, has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83ad96d22f37773114fd550dbd82d2bcd95e51fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$729$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> factors, but as long as you don't pull the unlucky d3 (if you choose one of these three options that give an available answer extraction), you actually will get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c6659f50a5772f1f9ea59fb561e96d38c6b9d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$441$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>~tiguhbabheow (I did make AIME)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Similar_to_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\">Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Similar to Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5be0e99d84e18484c14ae6fd549e13aac29504ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log_{2026} x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/6/fa69c6a323789bbd3403309a8d47cc64788c5962.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />. Then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143f1af35db6ad797d5f134e9fa5bf8ad6c2f72a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^y=2026^{y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e11ee6c85b3fc262585b6e87de47b65120bc2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{\\frac{y^2}{20}}=26\\cdot 2026^y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"156\" height=\"23\" />, which implies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c92b7e3e79aeda1637f21427e5234ccdd3e72013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{\\frac{y^2}{20-y}}=26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\nThus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae29ae9b20c5000ff36a7410c11d8b63c0c119dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y^2}{20-y}=\\log_{2026} 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"152\" height=\"44\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a3df920c12cc4d03f5f1750848c135b3cc10865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-20y-20\\log_{2026} 26=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"218\" height=\"21\" />.\nWe see that this quadratic has real solutions. Let the corresponding solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b111a4db0c13938d3027d905c1a37ee7a22e2373.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{y_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/64210cea8afdf24f70361ae4d59a9cb921f45418.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{y_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. Then the product of the solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/d/57ddfe2c9e83701a6e87b73cf1758e1ed8b3df6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{y_1+y_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />.\nBy Vieta’s formulas, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84dd73d822775f1c7eb294fc87ced25c1b21a654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1+y_2=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />, so the product of the solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73df736c4b5a91adb6986579917f0a43931aa466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />.\nFactoring, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c9ecbd48058e727c89d52faad9355c936d23d1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026=2\\cdot 1013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bbb3c4fbe4d662a50ef1f233bb0add32e263c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{20}=2^{20}\\cdot 1013^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"163\" height=\"17\" />, which has\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/7/f07e174ccae06a9e7820a77f560eae3744662c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20+1)(20+1)=441$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"20\" /> divisors.\n</p><p>~pl246631\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take the 20th power on both sides to obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1841669925d931ed36a1c043f1b61a744c93b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{\\log_{2026}x} = (26x)^{20}\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"20\" />\nGiven the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e33b79566627a389f03481df694a5722cabf23e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2026}(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, we find that this equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/57178ee8cabf7aecaeb146d6399785b194d02668.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2026^a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />. Thus the expression simplifies to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/4/0448a2f0242d1e538458103ec5d87909360f520a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2026^{a^2} = (26 \\cdot 2026^a)^{20}\\]\" width=\"177\" height=\"22\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe45c7e783fc576994234982c27576b580416d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2026^{a^2} = 26^{20} \\cdot 2026^{20a}\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />\nIn which we may divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f20a768690cba8d4aafeb9bbcbfa033c04fcbbd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{20a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> on both sides to obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea0cfd72b0cc8e9369aad86a0edb6f5c3f34777.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2026^{a^2}}{2026^{20a}} = 26^{20}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/188939177c5f647abacb759ef6d650bfd9cae654.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2026^{a^2 - 20a} = 26^{20}\\]\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" />\nTaking the logarithm base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e513adf78ee28ac3403e90a42259bc55f59e2d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> on both sides results in the quadratic\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f68fc4e67912220c41ea68c4a05b7e39f4d468dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 - 20a - \\log_{2026}(26^{20}) = 0\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"20\" />\nin simplest form is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7681e849aea26a83910a21c150182f9764f7de14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 - 20a - 20 \\log_{2026}(26) = 0.\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" />\nThe values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are determined by\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/ddeabc466c964a4bd2fc6a125e12c48efc6ddcaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\frac{20 \\pm \\sqrt{20^2 + 4 \\cdot 20 \\log_{2026}(26)}}{2}\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"41\" />\nNotice that the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> are equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5bd46e0e5c55665921392edf7b1c221958bb7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. We require <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f661930ed7b93aacf1c1c9e4e7ec7563ed4371.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in \\mathbb{R}^+$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, any real value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, positive or negative, is permitted. Thus two values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf0925be407694b51d525270da074be33141bbd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 2026^{a_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c99d316894b0fe114924b423cb71c9de79b89d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 = 2026^{a_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" /> exist. When we take their product, it is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad3de3c813213a0b2c900b26ebf1b9cf661cf18f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{a_1} \\cdot 2026^{a_2} = 2026^{a_1+a_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"216\" height=\"17\" />, in which we can see that the discriminant of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> cancels out. Thus, if we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c8b696db8f205bb5a743464538f25dec249236.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\sqrt{20^2 + 4 \\cdot 20 \\log_{2026}(26)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"226\" height=\"35\" />, then we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b29afb6f55b6ef526589cc7176bd438dda5fc444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = \\frac{20 + b}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"39\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/1223edf649c7483838db8fd381fb42f8c17c1a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 = \\frac{20 - b}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"39\" />, we see that the product of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73df736c4b5a91adb6986579917f0a43931aa466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Thus we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65fff4240491e477f271ebfda4ab611b803e19c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = 2026^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"17\" />, whose prime factorization is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8ed5ff0235e8c228f558b6a2f894fa4190eb769a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = 1013^{20} \\cdot 2^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"17\" />. The number of factors of a number with prime factorization <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9ab8867b7192d64e48cbbe9bde4d103ca4e477ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1^{e_1} \\cdot p_2^{e_2} \\cdot \\ldots \\cdot p_n^{e_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"19\" /> is determined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1639be3aef63818154b2a54486f0d74b2c01eebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(e_1+1)(e_2+1)\\ldots(e_n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, the number of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/51971f0c3bd6e6bff636d93ad7d8183c183b1688.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20+1)(20+1) = 21^2 = \\boxed{441}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"242\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b9a2a4d6eb635c4678db0f7abeea3d1a47894cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\log_{2026}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"19\" />. Raise both sides to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th power and take log base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e513adf78ee28ac3403e90a42259bc55f59e2d8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> of both sides.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/4312b3892b797aa4009a6f5f7f9863816f7f2b36.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{2026}(x^{\\log_{2026}x}) = \\log_{2026}(26x)^{20}\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"20\" />\nBy the power rule of logarithms we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d04d98099688c54fa84d19d0dcd1d6af576d42a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{2026}x \\cdot \\log_{2026}x = 20(\\log_{2026}(26 \\cdot x))\\]\" width=\"303\" height=\"18\" />\nBy the product rule of logarithms,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/acef3d0ed4ee63c5b86daa32e9357cc40799d0c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{2026}x \\cdot \\log_{2026}x = 20\\log_{2026}26 + 20\\log_{2026}x\\]\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa97d77b89717f551e8f040bbfafbe9c010d8219.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2 = 20y + 20\\log_{2026}26\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b636d3df4b019f2112bd1d495362cb2801ae600e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y^2 - 20y - 20\\log_{2026}26 = 0\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"20\" />\nLet's say the roots of this equation are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae250d1bdd46e5677f27edcf5efb34587b6fc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0320ab2ddd4939f9072e5316fe8888b0cddee319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" />, then the product of the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/7/447c207c08d8e9a81a3dafaa5fea90a78b0ce7e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2026^{y_1} \\cdot 2026^{y_2} = 2026^{y_1 + y_2}\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"15\" />\nBy Vieta's we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c8c026dfdd366fa9d03841abf44db08761f0fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1+y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"16\" /> is just 20, so the product of the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73df736c4b5a91adb6986579917f0a43931aa466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/8736f7a314cd28fb88b44c394672871fc3464d34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2026^{20} = 2^{20} \\cdot 1013^{20}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"15\" />\nSo the number of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b89b88e43463e4d148de5519fe372d6ccdea2129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2026^{20} (P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"21\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d4cbc819d282743e140090a9d95d40581d365b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20 + 1)(20 + 1) = 21^2 = \\boxed{441}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"242\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~midnightgalaxy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Fast_and_Easy_.F0.9F.94.A5.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Fast_and_Easy_🔥🚀)\">Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Fast and Easy 🔥🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a8UqbfoUmlM\">2026 AIME I #6</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://piacademyus.org/\">PiAcademyUs.org</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Easy)\">Video Solution (Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n6Jya5Jq58Y\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n6Jya5Jq58Y</a> - Continuum Math\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MadMath\">Video Solution by MadMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MadMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NAA6rmLeC4Q\">https://youtu.be/NAA6rmLeC4Q</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I\" title=\"2026 AIME I\">2026 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2026 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2026 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183426\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 644/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1451/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20221/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.925      1 Template:AIME_box\n100.00%   12.925      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35450:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017183426 and revision id 287051. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}